<div class="figma-page-content" style="font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:1.62;color:#0f172a;max-width:1080px;margin:0 auto;">
<h1 class="figma-screen-title">Objectives, the Three-Language Connection, and Pre-Check</h1>
<div class="figma-reading-card"><p style="font-size:17px;">A browser combines HTML, CSS, and JavaScript into one experience, but each language has a different responsibility. HTML describes what is on the page and how the content is organized. CSS describes how that content should look and how it should be arranged. JavaScript adds behavior, such as changing text after a visitor selects a button. Keeping these roles clear will help you decide where a change belongs when you build or debug a page.</p><p>By the end of the module, you should be able to identify the purpose of all three technologies, create the basic structure of a webpage with HTML, apply CSS to change appearance and layout, add one simple JavaScript interaction, and explain how the three pieces work together. The goal is a practical foundation, not memorization of every tag, property, or programming feature.</p><p>The short pre-check below is not graded. It simply helps you notice what you already know. If a question feels unfamiliar, that is expected; each answer will be covered later. After the pre-check, you will meet the embedded code editor and begin with the structural layer: HTML.</p></div>
<div class="figma-info-grid" style="">
<div style="flex:1 1 440px;background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;border-radius:13px;padding:17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size:20px;margin:0 0 8px;">Key ideas</h2><ul style="margin:0;padding-left:22px;"><li>HTML = structure and meaning.</li><li>CSS = presentation and layout.</li><li>JavaScript = behavior and interaction.</li><li>The browser combines all three into the page the learner sees.</li></ul>
</div>
<div style="flex:1 1 360px;background:#ecfeff;border:1px solid #99f6e4;border-radius:13px;padding:17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size:20px;margin:0 0 8px;color:#115e59;">Your task</h2><p style="margin:0;">Use the diagram as a mental model, then complete the three-question pre-check without looking anything up.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="margin:22px 0;"><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin:20px 0;">
<div style="padding:18px;border-radius:12px;background:#ecfeff;border:2px solid #0f766e;text-align:center;"><strong>HTML</strong><br/><span>Structure &amp; content</span></div>
<div aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:28px;text-align:center;">→</div>
<div style="padding:18px;border-radius:12px;background:#eff6ff;border:2px solid #2563eb;text-align:center;"><strong>CSS</strong><br/><span>Appearance &amp; layout</span></div>
<div aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:28px;text-align:center;">→</div>
<div style="padding:18px;border-radius:12px;background:#fff7ed;border:2px solid #b45309;text-align:center;"><strong>JavaScript</strong><br/><span>Behavior &amp; interaction</span></div>
</div><iframe loading="lazy" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-forms" src="{{context_path}}/content/resources/embeds/screen-02-quiz-01.html" style="width:100%;height:735px;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;border-radius:14px;background:#f8fafc;;border:1px solid #D9E1EC!important;border-radius:12px!important;background:#fff!important;" title="Short Pre-Check"></iframe></div>
<details style="margin:22px 0;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;background:white;">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;font-weight:700;color:#0f766e;">Quick check: What question should you ask when deciding which language to use?</summary>
<p style="margin:12px 0 0;">Ask whether the change concerns structure/content, visual presentation, or behavior.</p>
</details>
<div class="figma-footer-line" style="padding-top:13px;border-top:1px solid #e2e8f0;color:#64748b;font-size:13px;">Basics in Webpage Making · Screen 2 of 20</div>
</div>","textFeedbackInput":"Show Feedback","textFeedbackTextarea":"","textInfoDurationInput":"","textInfoDurationTextInput":"Duration","textInfoParticipantsInput":"","textInfoParticipantsTextInput":"Grouping"}

