<div class="figma-page-content" style="font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:1.62;color:#0f172a;max-width:1080px;margin:0 auto;">
<h1 class="figma-screen-title">Meet the Embedded Code Editor</h1>
<div class="figma-reading-card"><p style="font-size:17px;">The embedded editor lets you practice without installing software. It has three code areas—HTML, CSS, and JavaScript—and an output preview. During the HTML section, your attention will stay mostly on the HTML pane. The CSS and JavaScript panes may already contain a small amount of supporting code, but you do not need to understand those parts yet.</p><p>The preview updates after you type, and the Run button lets you refresh it immediately. Reset restores the starter code for the current activity. Reset is useful when several changes make the example difficult to repair. An error does not mean you failed; it is information. Compare the code with the example, check punctuation and closing tags, and try again.</p><p>This module uses the same small webpage repeatedly. That means code from one stage will appear again later with new additions. You are not expected to preserve your edits from one screen to the next. Each activity starts with the version needed for that lesson, allowing you to focus on the new concept without rebuilding everything.</p></div>
<div class="figma-info-grid" style="">
<div style="flex:1 1 440px;background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;border-radius:13px;padding:17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size:20px;margin:0 0 8px;">Key ideas</h2><ul style="margin:0;padding-left:22px;"><li>Edit code in the labeled pane.</li><li>Use Run to refresh the output immediately.</li><li>Use Reset to return to the activity's starter code.</li><li>Read error messages and inspect the smallest recent change first.</li></ul>
</div>
<div style="flex:1 1 360px;background:#ecfeff;border:1px solid #99f6e4;border-radius:13px;padding:17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size:20px;margin:0 0 8px;color:#115e59;">Your task</h2><p style="margin:0;">Change “My Web Learning Page” to a title of your choice, then change the paragraph. Confirm that the preview changes while the CSS and JavaScript panes remain untouched.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="margin:22px 0;"><iframe class="figma-code-lab" loading="lazy" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-forms allow-modals allow-popups" src="{{context_path}}/content/resources/embeds/screen-03-editor-01.html" style="width:100%;height:680px;border:0;border-radius:14px;background:#f8fafc;display:block;" title="Interactive code editor: Editor Orientation"></iframe></div>
<details style="margin:22px 0;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;background:white;">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;font-weight:700;color:#0f766e;">Quick check: What should you use if you want the original activity code back?</summary>
<p style="margin:12px 0 0;">Use Reset. It restores the starter code for that activity.</p>
</details>
<div class="figma-footer-line" style="padding-top:13px;border-top:1px solid #e2e8f0;color:#64748b;font-size:13px;">Basics in Webpage Making · Screen 3 of 20</div>
</div>","textFeedbackInput":"Show Feedback","textFeedbackTextarea":"","textInfoDurationInput":"","textInfoDurationTextInput":"Duration","textInfoParticipantsInput":"","textInfoParticipantsTextInput":"Grouping"}

