<div class="figma-page-content" style="font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:1.62;color:#0f172a;max-width:1080px;margin:0 auto;">
<h1 class="figma-screen-title">HTML Guided Practice and Knowledge Check</h1>
<div class="figma-reading-card"><p style="font-size:17px;">You have now seen the major HTML pieces needed for the course project. This screen gives you a chance to apply them together before moving to CSS. Begin by reading the existing structure rather than immediately typing. Identify the head, body, header, main content, sections, links, image, list, and footer. Being able to recognize structure is as important as being able to create it.</p><p>For the guided practice, personalize the webpage while preserving its organization. Change the page title and main heading, rewrite one paragraph, add a third resource link, and verify that the image still has meaningful alternative text. If the preview changes unexpectedly, inspect the tag you changed most recently. Look for a missing closing angle bracket, quotation mark, or end tag.</p><p>After practicing, complete the knowledge check. The questions focus on the purpose of the HTML elements used in this project. A perfect score is not required to continue, but if you miss a question, use the feedback to return to the relevant example. CSS will depend on the HTML structure you have just built, so this is a good point to confirm the foundation.</p></div>
<div class="figma-info-grid" style="">
<div style="flex:1 1 440px;background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;border-radius:13px;padding:17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size:20px;margin:0 0 8px;">Key ideas</h2><ul style="margin:0;padding-left:22px;"><li>Recognize the document structure before editing it.</li><li>Keep visible content inside the body.</li><li>Use meaningful headings, links, and image alternatives.</li><li>Debug the most recent small change first.</li></ul>
</div>
<div style="flex:1 1 360px;background:#ecfeff;border:1px solid #99f6e4;border-radius:13px;padding:17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size:20px;margin:0 0 8px;color:#115e59;">Your task</h2><p style="margin:0;">Complete the HTML edits, then answer all four knowledge-check questions.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="margin:22px 0;"><iframe class="figma-code-lab" loading="lazy" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-forms allow-modals allow-popups" src="{{context_path}}/content/resources/embeds/screen-06-editor-01.html" style="width:100%;height:680px;border:0;border-radius:14px;background:#f8fafc;display:block;" title="Interactive code editor: HTML Guided Practice"></iframe><iframe loading="lazy" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-forms" src="{{context_path}}/content/resources/embeds/screen-06-quiz-02.html" style="width:100%;height:880px;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;border-radius:14px;background:#f8fafc;;border:1px solid #D9E1EC!important;border-radius:12px!important;background:#fff!important;" title="HTML Knowledge Check"></iframe></div>
<details style="margin:22px 0;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;background:white;">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;font-weight:700;color:#0f766e;">Quick check: What is the main job of HTML in this project?</summary>
<p style="margin:12px 0 0;">HTML provides the content, structure, and meaning of the webpage.</p>
</details>
